description:
Organize the layout sections within bundle.css for better maintainability.

## Current State
CSS is now bundled into css/bundle.css (5240 lines). The layout styles (originally 758 lines from layout.css) handle both desktop (≥769px) and mobile (≤768px) but are interleaved.

## Proposed Organization
Within bundle.css, reorganize layout sections using CSS comments or @layer:

```css
/* ========== LAYOUT: SHARED ========== */
/* Base layout styles used by both breakpoints */

/* ========== LAYOUT: DESKTOP (≥769px) ========== */
@media (min-width: 769px) { ... }

/* ========== LAYOUT: MOBILE (≤768px) ========== */
@media (max-width: 768px) { ... }
```

## Benefits
- Easier to find and modify breakpoint-specific styles
- Clear separation of concerns within single file
- Maintains bundling performance benefits

## Alternative
If bundle.css grows unwieldy, consider CSS @layer for logical grouping without separate files.

## Files
- css/bundle.css - Layout sections to organize
